{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, Oksana. Come on in. Before anything else, can you give me your full name and date of birth?",
   "start": 0.11,
   "end": 8.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Oksana Kovalenko, August 30, 1979.",
   "start": 9.1,
   "end": 12.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thank you. How's the soryasi spin?",
   "start": 13.36,
   "end": 16.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Honestly, worse. Over the last four months, it's spread. My elbows and knees are bad again, there's a big patch on my lower back, and my scalp itches like crazy. I've had this for eight years, and this is the worst it's been.",
   "start": 16.8,
   "end": 29.58
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'm sorry. Are you still using the clobetasol ointment?",
   "start": 30.22,
   "end": 35.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, twice a day on the worst spots. It helps for a few days, and then it all comes back.",
   "start": 36.16,
   "end": 40.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And the methotrexate from last spring?",
   "start": 41.44,
   "end": 44.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I stopped that on my own in June. I was on 10 milligrams a week. No, wait, it was 15, 6 of the little 2 .5 pills. It made me so nauseous, and my hair got thin.",
   "start": 44.76,
   "end": 55.6
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, that's helpful. Thank you for telling me. Let me ask about your any joint pain or swelling. Stiffness in the morning. Sausage -like swelling of a finger or toe. Heal pain.",
   "start": 55.6,
   "end": 75.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, none of that. My mom had rheumatoid arthritis in her hands, so I'd notice, believe me.",
   "start": 76.1,
   "end": 81.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good. Other medicines.",
   "start": 81.86,
   "end": 83.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Amlodipine. 5 milligrams every morning for blood pressure.",
   "start": 84.2,
   "end": 87.32
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's it. And you're allergic to Sulfa.",
   "start": 87.9,
   "end": 90.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, I get a rash all over.",
   "start": 92.71,
   "end": 93.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Still not smoking.",
   "start": 94.69,
   "end": 95.69
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Three years quit now.",
   "start": 96.7,
   "end": 97.68
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's great. Okay. You're well -defined with thick silvery scale. The right one is about eight by six centimeters. Similar pla - seven centimeters. That's scaly pla - I see pitting on three of your fingernails. Your finger joints aren't swollen or toe swollen fingers.",
   "start": 98.62,
   "end": 139.45
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Twelve percent. That sounds like a lot.",
   "start": 146.78,
   "end": 148.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "It is. So this is moderate to severe plaque psoriasis that isn't controlled with creams. And methotrex... I think you're a really good candle, is Rissing Kizumab. It's an injection under the skin, 150 milligrams, given at week zero, week four, every 12 weeks.",
   "start": 148.78,
   "end": 182.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Every 12 weeks? That's not bad. What are the risks? It",
   "start": 182.85,
   "end": 186.17
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "calms down a slightly higher chance of in like colds, serious problems. Before we start, TB blood should also avoid live vaccines once you're on it. So getting your flu shot this fall is a good idea.",
   "start": 186.58,
   "end": 218.53
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, can I do the blood work at the lab by my house? It's at 2 ,250 Riverside Drive.",
   "start": 219.15,
   "end": 225.15
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Absolutely, I'll send the orders there. Also need authorization, your insurance.",
   "start": 225.93,
   "end": 233.59
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, member ID is K, as in kilo 7 -0 -3 -9 -2 -1 -5.",
   "start": 236.06,
   "end": 241.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Keep the clobetasol ointment twice a day, on the skin doesn't thin. For your scalp, I'm adding clobetasol 0 .05 % solution. Once a day at night.",
   "start": 244.94,
   "end": 266.07
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, my husband Taras will be thrilled. He's tired of the flakes on the couch.",
   "start": 266.9,
   "end": 270.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "If you ever do get joint pain, swelling, Soryasi's up results.",
   "start": 272.67,
   "end": 290.26
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "5 5 5 0 1 3 4.",
   "start": 290.48,
   "end": 294.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great. Once the labs and insurance approval come best injection. Eyes follow up in six weeks.",
   "start": 294.26,
   "end": 308.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thank you Dr. Nair. I'm actually hopeful.",
   "start": 309.25,
   "end": 311.43
  }
